title: git_odb_new is bound with a repository argument it does not take; the result
  is an empty ODB
updated: 2026-10-25T01:27:55Z
---

`lib/Git/Libgit2/FFI.pm:505`: `_attach git_odb_new => [ 'opaque*', 'git_repository' ] => 'int';`, POD `FFI.pm:2128-2132`: `git_odb_new(\my $odb, $repo)` - "Create a new ODB wrapper".

libgit2 declares `int git_odb_new(git_odb **odb)` (`git2/odb.h:102`; the two-argument form at `odb.h:74` is the experimental-SHA256 variant and takes `const git_odb_options *`, not a repository). The call creates a fresh object database with **no backends**; the C side never looks at `$repo`. `git_odb_exists($odb, $oid)` on that handle answers 0 for every object in the repository. The function that returns the repository's ODB is `git_repository_odb`, bound correctly at `FFI.pm:134`.

No test touches `git_odb_new`, `git_odb_exists` or `git_odb_free` (`grep -rn odb t/` is empty), so nothing noticed.

Done when: `git_odb_new` is bound as `[ 'opaque*' ]` and documented as "empty ODB, add backends yourself" (or removed), the ODB POD section points at `git_repository_odb`, and a test opens the repository ODB and checks `git_odb_exists` for a present and an absent oid.

